{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #11 in user/delegate: `delegate models`, a trimmed `delegate doctor`, and the new model table. Read the ticket (`gh issue view 11`) and its owner rulings (`gh issue view 11 --comments`), plus the #7 rulings (`gh issue view 7 --comments`). The spec is issue #4. Follow the repo's AGENTS.md. Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no delegate tools. Stay on branch `11-models-doctor` in this worktree. Do not create branches and do not push.\n\n## File fence\nOwns:\n- config/models.json\n- src/models.rs, src/config.rs, src/doctor.rs, src/doctor_tests.rs\n- src/types.rs: only `ModelEntry`, `ResolvedModel` and `Price`\n- new src/cli_info.rs for `models` and `doctor`, plus its `mod` line in src/lib.rs\n- new tests/cli_info_e2e.rs\n- src/index/tests.rs, src/runner/tests.rs, tests/e2e.rs: model-id updates only\n\nIn src/cli.rs you may change only three things:\n- add the `Some(\"models\")` and `Some(\"doctor\")` dispatch arms in `main`\n- add their lines to `USAGE`\n- in `run`, change the `resolve_model(...).is_err()` block so it prints the actual error. Keep the \"valid models: ...\" id list for an unknown id.\n\nEverything else is forbidden: the rest of src/cli.rs, src/gate.rs, src/git.rs, lock code, and .github/. Another lane is editing the rest of src/cli.rs in parallel. If you need a file outside the fence, stop and report.\n\n## Model table\n`backend` replaces `family` everywhere. Its values are \"cursor\", \"pi\" and \"claude\". The MCP `requireNonClaude` check becomes `backend == \"claude\"`. Default: `composer-2.5`.\n\nPrices are $ per 1M tokens, written as input / output / cacheRead / cacheWrite:\n\n| id | label | backend | input | output | cacheRead | cacheWrite |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| composer-2.5 | Composer 2.5 | cursor | 0.5 | 2.5 | 0.2 | 0 |\n| grok-4.7-high | Grok 4.7 High | cursor | 2 | 6 | 0.5 | 0 |\n| grok-4.7-xhigh | Grok 4.7 Extra High | cursor | 2 | 6 | 0.5 | 0 |\n| opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor | Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor | pi | 0.1 | 0.2 | 0.002 | 0 |\n| opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash | GLM 5.3 Flash | pi | 0.15 | 0.5 | 0.03 | 0 |\n| opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash | pi | 0.15 | 0.6 | 0.003 | 0 |\n| openai-codex/gpt-6-astra | GPT-6 Astra | pi | 10 | 50 | 1 | 12.5 |\n| openai-codex/gpt-6-luna | GPT-6 Luna | pi | 0.1 | 0.5 | 0.01 | 0.125 |\n| openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol | GPT-6.1 Sol | pi | 2 | 10 | 0.1 | 2.5 |\n| claude-opus-5-5 | Claude Opus 5.5 | claude | 4 | 20 | 0.2 | 5 |\n| claude-sonnet-5-5 | Claude Sonnet 5.5 | claude | 2 | 10 | 0.2 | 2.5 |\n| claude-fable-5-1 | Claude Fable 5.1 | claude | 10 | 50 | 0.25 | 12.5 |\n\nDelete the old ids (cursor-grok-4.5/4.6-*, gemini-3.5-flash, gpt-5.6-*). Every test that used them moves to the new ids.\n\n## Backend gate\npi and claude are not implemented yet. `resolve_model` (the code that `run` and MCP already call) returns an error for them, worded exactly:\n`model \"claude-sonnet-5-5\" uses backend \"claude\", which is not implemented yet`\n`delegate run` prints that on stderr and exits 2.\n\n## `delegate models`\nAn aligned text table on stdout, exit 0. Rows sort by backend, then by id. A `*` marks the default. Prices are $ per 1M tokens, shown as input/output. Two of the literal rows, with the header:\n```\n  ID                                       LABEL                       BACKEND  $IN/1M  $OUT/1M\n* composer-2.5                             Composer 2.5                cursor     0.50     2.50\n  opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor   Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor  pi         0.10     0.20\n```\nExact column widths are yours. Size them to the longest value.\n\n## `delegate doctor`\nHuman text on stdout, one line per check, with a status word padded to 5 columns. Exit 0 when the only problems are warnings, and exit 1 on any `fail`. Literal examples:\n```\nok    delegate 0.5.0\nok    cursor: cursor-agent 2026.09.28-64d2043 (/Users/u/.local/bin/cursor-agent)\nok    cursor: logged in\nwarn  cursor: model grok-4.7-xhigh missing from cursor-agent --list-models\nskip  pi: backend not implemented (6 models)\nskip  claude: backend not implemented (3 models)\nfail  cursor: cursor-agent not found\n```\nFor cursor, doctor checks that the binary is found, its version, the login (via `about`), and each cursor model against `--list-models`. Reuse the existing doctor.rs helpers. Delete the plugin-registration, legacy-name and deny-list checks, and their tests. The MCP server's doctor tool may keep its JSON shape, but it must still compile and pass.\n\n## Tests\nWrite the e2e tests first (TDD) in tests/cli_info_e2e.rs. Drive `CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate` as a process against a fake cursor-agent shell script, following the pattern in tests/cli_e2e.rs. Cover:\n- `models` lists all 12 ids, with the default marked\n- `doctor` passes with exit 0 against a fake agent that lists every cursor model\n- `doctor` prints a warn line and still exits 0 when the fake omits `grok-4.7-xhigh`\n- `doctor` fails with exit 1 when the binary is missing\n- `run --model claude-sonnet-5-5` exits 2 with the not-implemented message\n\nBefore you commit, all of these must pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo test`.\n\n## Finish\nCommit with a conventional message ending `Co-Authored-By: Muse Spark 1.3 <noreply@opencode.ai>`. Do not push.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA and the `cargo test` summary line, or a failure triage, and nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, and what you'd change (\"none\" is fine).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}],"timestamp":1790845529730}}
