{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_01a0f6b68fa873c68146def8ffbac5ea|fc_01a0f6b68fa873c68146def8ffbac5ea","toolName":"read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"use std::process::Command;\n\npub fn resolve_cursor_bin(r#override: Option<&str>) -> String {\n    if let Some(o) = r#override.filter(|s| !s.is_empty()) {\n        return o.to_string();\n    }\n    if let Ok(env) = std::env::var(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\")\n        && !env.is_empty()\n    {\n        return env;\n    }\n    if let Ok(out) = Command::new(\"which\").arg(\"cursor-agent\").output()\n        && out.status.success()\n    {\n        let found = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).trim().to_string();\n        if !found.is_empty() {\n            return found;\n        }\n    }\n    crate::util::homedir()\n        .join(\".local/bin/cursor-agent\")\n        .to_string_lossy()\n        .into_owned()\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn explicit_override_wins() {\n        assert_eq!(\n            resolve_cursor_bin(Some(\"/custom/cursor-agent\")),\n            \"/custom/cursor-agent\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn env_used_when_no_override() {\n        let prev = std::env::var(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\").ok();\n        unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", \"/env/cursor-agent\") };\n        assert_eq!(resolve_cursor_bin(None), \"/env/cursor-agent\");\n        match prev {\n            Some(v) => unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", v) },\n            None => unsafe { std::env::remove_var(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\") },\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}]},"isError":false}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_01a0f6b69150713f808e4987680fc0ab|fc_01a0f6b69150713f808e4987680fc0ab","toolName":"read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"fn main() {\n    std::process::exit(cursor_delegate_mcp::cli::main());\n}\n"}]},"isError":false}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a0f6b68ddd77c8a82d2b5d3d98eec4|fc_01a0f6b68ddd77c8a82d2b5d3d98eec4","toolName":"grep","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CODE-REVIEW.md:18: **Fix:** Clear the idle timer when the child closes (in the backend `done`/`close` path or at the top of `finalizeJob`), before finalize runs.\nCODE-REVIEW.md:107: - **Unbounded buffer growth** — `src/backends/cursor.ts:50,61`: `stderrBuf` (and `stdoutBuf` for a newline-less stream) accumulate for the child's whole lifetime, though finalize keeps only the last 2,048 bytes. Use a rolling tail for long/chatty jobs.\nREADME.md:12:   a `family` tag, and `$/MTok` prices. A model is callable iff it is in the map; the `model` enum\nREADME.md:15: - **Uncorrelated review contract** — `requireNonClaude: true` **hard-rejects** if the resolved\nREADME.md:16:   model's family is `claude` (no silent swap), so a reviewer never shares the producer's family.\nREADME.md:79: | `config/models.json` (bundled) | model allow-list: `default` + per-id `{label, family, price}` (`$/MTok`) |\nspec.md:22:   labels, family tags, and hand-maintained `$/MTok` prices. A model is callable iff it is in the\nspec.md:23:   map; the MCP `model` enum is generated from that map at startup. Optional `requireNonClaude`\nspec.md:24:   hard-rejects when the resolved model's `family === \"claude\"` (no silent swap).\nspec.md:65: job_registry.rs ..... STATEFUL. spawn via backend, deadline-race, detach+jobId,\nspec.md:68:    ├── backends/cursor.rs ... spawn cursor-agent, parse stream-json (NDJSON) lines,\nspec.md:69:    │      backends/types.rs    emit \"progress\"/\"stderr\" events, resolve a BackendResult\nspec.md:78:    models.rs ....... model id → ResolvedModel (+ requireNonClaude hard reject)\nspec.md:111:   requireNonClaude?: boolean;  // hard-reject if resolved family === \"claude\"\nspec.md:143:   backend: string;               // \"cursor\"\nspec.md:168: interface ModelEntry { label: string; family: string; price: Price; }\nspec.md:170: interface ResolvedModel { model: string; family: string; price: Price; }\nspec.md:175:   requireNonClaude?: boolean;\nspec.md:242: 1. Resolve model from `{model, requireNonClaude}` against the curated map.\nspec.md:289:    `ResumeContext` fields (`model`, `requireNonClaude`, `capability`, `allowUnsandboxed`,\nspec.md:414: 2. Generate a UUID jobId; `backend.run(spec)` spawns the child and returns `{child, events, done}`.\nspec.md:441: On child close the backend resolves `{ raw, cleanExit, stderr }`. `finalizeJob`:\nspec.md:474: | `config/models.json` (bundled) | curated allow-list: `{ default, models: { <id>: { label, family, price } } }` |\nspec.md:516:     \"composer-2.5\":     { \"label\": \"Composer 2.5\",    \"family\": \"composer\", \"price\": { \"input\": 0.5, \"output\": 2.5, \"cacheRead\": 0.2,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nspec.md:517:     \"grok-4.5-xhigh\":   { \"label\": \"Grok 4.5\",         \"family\": \"grok\",     \"price\": { \"input\": 2,   \"output\": 6,   \"cacheRead\": 0.5,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nspec.md:518:     \"gemini-3.5-flash\": { \"label\": \"Gemini 3.5 Flash\", \"family\": \"gemini\",   \"price\": { \"input\": 1.5, \"output\": 9,   \"cacheRead\": 0.15, \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nspec.md:519:     \"gpt-5.5-high\":     { \"label\": \"GPT-5.5 1M High\",  \"family\": \"gpt\",      \"price\": { \"input\": 5,   \"output\": 30,  \"cacheRead\": 0.5,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } }\nspec.md:523: Prices are `$/MTok`, hand-maintained (the CLI exposes no pricing). `family` is a free string; the\nspec.md:533: `resolveModel({ model, requireNonClaude }, { default, models })`:\nspec.md:536: 3. If `requireNonClaude` and `entry.family === \"claude\"` → throw `NonClaudeViolationError`\nspec.md:538: 4. Return `{ model, family: entry.family, price: entry.price }`.\nspec.md:657: - `makeJobRegistry({ backend: makeCursorAdapter(), deadlineMs: cfg.profile.deadlineMs ?? 60000,\nspec.md:685: | #9 | Per-call `idleMs`/`toolIdleMs` overrides; tiered idle watchdog (`phase`-aware: wider window while a tool call is in flight); raw stdout `activity` also re-arms; CANCELLED/STALLED still compute the change-set (`finalizeStall`, skips only gate + incomplete-commit) and `text` summarizes the job's last known progress instead of being empty | `job_registry.rs`, `stream.rs`, `backends/cursor.rs`, `finalize.rs`, `runner.rs`, `tool_schemas.rs` |\nspec.md:693: are `model` + `requireNonClaude` (not symbolic selectors). The governing principle: *never review an\nspec.md:694: agent's output with the same model that produced it.* Reviewer roles pass `requireNonClaude: true`\nspec.md:696: `requireNonClaude: true`, `ask`), **Triager** (`composer-2.5`, `ask`), **Design-critic**\nspec.md:697: (`gemini-3.5-flash`, `requireNonClaude: true`, `plan`), **Codemod** / **Re-implementer** /\nspec.md:699: spec/quality reviewers** (different allow-list engines from the implementer, `requireNonClaude:\nspec.md:768: - unknown model id → `ModelNotAllowedError`; `requireNonClaude` + Claude family →\nconfig/models.json:4:     \"composer-2.5\":     { \"label\": \"Composer 2.5\",    \"family\": \"composer\", \"price\": { \"input\": 0.5, \"output\": 2.5, \"cacheRead\": 0.2,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nconfig/models.json:5:     \"cursor-grok-4.5-high\":   { \"label\": \"Grok 4.5\",         \"family\": \"grok\",     \"price\": { \"input\": 2,   \"output\": 6,   \"cacheRead\": 0.5,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nconfig/models.json:6:     \"cursor-grok-4.6-high\":   { \"label\": \"Grok 4.6\",         \"family\": \"grok\",     \"price\": { \"input\": 2,   \"output\": 6,   \"cacheRead\": 0.5,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nconfig/models.json:7:     \"cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh\":  { \"label\": \"Grok 4.6 Extra High\", \"family\": \"grok\",     \"price\": { \"input\": 2,   \"output\": 6,   \"cacheRead\": 0.5,  \"cacheWrite\": 0 } },\nconfig/models.json:8:     \"gemini-3.5-flash\": { \"label\": \"Gemini 3.5 Flash\", \"family\": \"gemini\",   \"price\": { \"input\